{
  "name": "Warm match cache (sub-workflow)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "0e0e0e0e-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "name": "About this workflow",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -32,
        -448
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 1184,
        "height": 224,
        "content": "## Warm match cache (called by A after every crawl)\nJudges, before any batch arrives, every cohort the active products can produce (`cohort_space()`, enumerated from the products alone) and compiles every fuzzy criterion that has no rule yet, through the same request builder and LLM gateway as Workflow B. A batch then finds everything cached, so **Workflow B makes no LLM call at match time**.\nUnder threshold banding the space is exactly what batches produce, so this costs no extra calls. With nothing new it is one query and no request. A failure here never fails the crawl: Workflow B still judges anything uncached itself."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "0e0e0e0e-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
      "name": "Called by A",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.executeWorkflowTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "inputSource": "passthrough"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "0e0e0e0e-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
      "name": "Run manually",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.manualTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        192
      ],
      "parameters": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "0e0e0e0e-0000-4000-8000-000000000005",
      "name": "Find unjudged cohorts",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.postgres",
